      "writtenOn": "2026-03-11T23:26:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Optional: I found that these two functions share a lot of code. We can move the middle part of this function to a helper function:\n\n```\n// Return 0 to indicate the cost should not be adjusted.\nstatic int64_t get_var_offset(const AV1_COMP *cpi, const MACROBLOCK *x) {\n  if (cpi-\u003eoxcf.algo_cfg.sharpness !\u003d 3) return 0;\n\n  if (frame_is_kf_gf_arf(cpi)) return 0;\n\n  int64_t src_var, rec_var;\n  const bool is_hbd \u003d is_cur_buf_hbd(\u0026x-\u003ee_mbd);\n\n  if (is_hbd)\n    get_variance_stats_hbd(x, \u0026src_var, \u0026rec_var);\n  else\n    get_variance_stats(x, \u0026src_var, \u0026rec_var);\n\n  if (src_var \u003c\u003d rec_var) return 0;\n\n  return src_var - rec_var;\n}\n```\n\nThen these two functions (before your changes) would become:\n\n```\nstatic void adjust_rdcost(const AV1_COMP *cpi, const MACROBLOCK *x,\n                          RD_STATS *rd_cost) {\n  int64_t var_offset \u003d get_var_offset(cpi, x);\n  if (var_offset \u003d\u003d 0) return;\n\n  rd_cost-\u003edist +\u003d var_offset;\n\n  rd_cost-\u003erdcost \u003d RDCOST(x-\u003erdmult, rd_cost-\u003erate, rd_cost-\u003edist);\n}\n\nstatic void adjust_cost(const AV1_COMP *cpi, const MACROBLOCK *x,\n                        int64_t *rd_cost) {\n  int64_t var_offset \u003d get_var_offset(cpi, x);\n  if (var_offset \u003d\u003d 0) return;\n\n  *rd_cost +\u003d RDCOST(x-\u003erdmult, 0, var_offset);\n}                    \n```\n\nDo you think this is worth doing (in a separate CL)?",
      "revId": "8a6ad1a31b4baf101fa51da229e5786eaded4661",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
