    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "05271ff0_98ee3b1f",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/rdopt.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1855,
      "author": {
        "id": 9545
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-12T00:43:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`thid_yrd` is assigned a value here. We reach here if `do_tx_search` is true.",
      "revId": "8a6ad1a31b4baf101fa51da229e5786eaded4661",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "31ef4154_8c1cf2bd",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/rdopt.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1878,
      "author": {
        "id": 9545
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-12T00:43:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Therefore, if `do_tx_search` is false, `this_yrd` is equal to `INT64_MAX` when we pass it to `adjust_cost()`. So the addition to `this_yrd` inside `adjust_cost()` may overflow!\n\nThis means `adjust_cost()` needs to handle overflow, e.g, by using saturating arithmetic.",
      "revId": "8a6ad1a31b4baf101fa51da229e5786eaded4661",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cbfcafe4_11c3ff5e",
        "filename": "av1/encoder/rdopt.c",
        "patchSetId": 8
      },
      "lineNbr": 1878,
      "author": {
        "id": 3678645
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-03-12T17:41:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm, you have a good point.\n\nIf I understand libaom\u0027s code correctly: `INT64_MAX` is used for RDO costs to either mark block candidates as invalid, or to signal that a search didn\u0027t find a block candidate (or in this case, the search was skipped). Otherwise, RDO costs for valid candidates aren\u0027t meant to get even close to overflowing the 64-bit int variable.\n\nThis means for `adjust_cost()` we could simply do:\n```\nif (cost \u003d\u003d INT64_MAX) return;\n```\n\nWith this CL, I\u0027m only biasing the costs of inter candidates by 1.125x, so doing it in the way above should be reasonable.",
      "parentUuid": "31ef4154_8c1cf2bd",
      "revId": "8a6ad1a31b4baf101fa51da229e5786eaded4661",
      "serverId": "e5514cf8-2d6e-3e29-adb4-24cd6dde4bf0"
    },
